     E_{1H} = \frac{3}{5} \frac{Z(Z-1) e^{2}}{4 \pi \varepsilon_{0} R}
     \]
     Given:
     \[
     Z_{1H} = 1, \quad e^{2} = 1.44 \text{ MeV} \text{fm}
     \]
     \[
     \varepsilon_{0} = 931.5 \text{ MeV/c}^2
     \]
     \[
     R = 1 \text{ fm} = 10^{-15} \text{ m}
     \]
     \[
     R_{1H} = 1 \text{ fm}
     \]
     \[
     E_{1H} = \frac{3}{5} \frac{1(1-1) \cdot 1.44 \text{ MeV} \text{fm}}{4 \pi \cdot 931.5 \text{ MeV/c}^2 \cdot 10^{-15} \text{ m}}
     \]
